/title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/asteroidshield-logo</link><description>从天空中保卫地球 - 佩戴救生艇基金会 AsteroidShield 并与行星守护者站在一起。&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/logo.asteroidshield-logo2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 01:06:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/asteroidshield-logo</guid></item><item><title>研究人员利用光产生纳米级磁化</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/researchers-use-light-to-generate-nanoscale-magnetization</link><description>康奈尔大学的研究人员利用一种捕获光的工程超表面，展示了一种无需使用外部磁铁或磁性材料即可产生强静磁场的新方法，这种方法可以推进自旋电子学、量子和光子计算以及数据存储。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/researchers-use-light-to-generate-nanoscale-magnetization.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 00:51:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/researchers-use-light-to-generate-nanoscale-magnetization</guid></item><item><title>模拟表明暗物质并不是恒星流的怪点</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/simulations-show-that-dark-matter-isnt-what-gives-stellar-streams-their-kinks</link><description>天文学家通过模拟银河系周围的恒星流来研究暗物质。他们发现这些流中的扭结和团块并不是由银河晕内的暗物质团引起的。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/simulations-show-that-dark-matter-isnt-what-gives-stellar-streams-their-kinks.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 00:36:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/simulations-show-that-dark-matter-isnt-what-gives-stellar-streams-their-kinks</guid></item><item><title>突破有助于扩大遗传字母表</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/breakthrough-helps-expand-genetic-alphabet</link><description>地球上所有已知的生命都使用相同的遗传字母表，由四个字母组成。现在，加州大学圣地亚哥分校的研究人员已经证明，生物学中最重要的酶之一可以准确读取和转录扩展的八个字母的遗传字母表。这些发现提供了重要证据，表明细胞可以利用其天然分子机制处理合成遗传信息，从而推进合成生物学扩展 DNA 语言的长期目标。它还可以让科学家定制工程生物系统来执行功能或生产自然界中未发现的化合物。&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/breakthrough-helps-expand-genetic-alphabet.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 00:21:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/breakthrough-helps-expand-genetic-alphabet</guid></item><item><title>约克航天公司推出用于极低轨道任务的卫星巴士</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/york-space-unveils-satellite-bus-for-missions-in-very-low-orbit</link><description>约克航天公司推出用于极低轨道任务的卫星巴士&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/york-space-unveils-satellite-bus-for-missions-in-very-low-orbit2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 00:06:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/york-space-unveils-satellite-bus-for-missions-in-very-low-orbit</guid></item><item><title>研究人员打造了一款价值 7 美元的智能手机夹子，可以发现隐藏摄像头动态 LED 网格，准确率达 94%</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/researchers-build-a-7-smartphone-clipon-that-spots-hidden-cameras-dynamic-led-grid-deliver-94-accuracy</link><description>这是AI工具的一个很好的用途。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/researchers-build-a-7-smartphone-clipon-that-spots-hidden-cameras-dynamic-led-grid-deliver-94-accuracy.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 23:51:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/researchers-build-a-7-smartphone-clipon-that-spots-hidden-cameras-dynamic-led-grid-deliver-94-accuracy</guid></item><item><title>1600 年左右，一位英国先驱医生和自然哲学家发明了第一台验电器——佛索里姆，并检测到静电荷的存在</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/around-1600-a-pioneering-english-physician-and-natural-philosopher-invented-versorium-the-first-electroscope-and-detected-the-presence-of-static-electric-charges</link><description>1600 年左右，William Gilbert 发明了 Versorium，第一台验电器，用于检测静电荷。这位英国医生和自然哲学家通过实验研究电和磁。他的工作有助于将磁性与静电分开。他还认为地球是一个巨大的磁铁，并用土来展示磁性行为的工作原理。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/around-1600-a-pioneering-english-physician-and-natural-philosopher-invented-versorium-the-first-electroscope-and-detected-the-presence-of-static-electric-charges.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 23:36:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/around-1600-a-pioneering-english-physician-and-natural-philosopher-invented-versorium-the-first-electroscope-and-detected-the-presence-of-static-electric-charges</guid></item></channel></rss>